<body>
    <h1>Best Practices for Computer Vision</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-Introduction">Introduction=
</h2>
<p>Adopting best practices when developing computer vision applications wit=
h Apple=E2=80=99s Vision Framework is essential to ensure quality, scalabil=
ity, maintainability, and a smooth user experience. Projects involving anyt=
hing from object detection to text recognition and integration with machine=
 learning models require code that is well-organized, efficient, and secure=
.</p>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-ArchitectureandCodeOrganization">A=
rchitecture and Code Organization</h2>
<p>Well-structured applications make it easier to maintain and evolve featu=
res. Patterns like <strong>Model-View-ViewModel (MVVM)</strong> and others =
help separate data logic, interface, and presentation.</p>
<p>Dedicated services such as <code>FaceDetectionService</code> or <code>Te=
xtRecognitionService</code> allow for encapsulating <code>VNRequest</code>c=
alls, keeping the code modular and reusable.</p>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-CombiningVisionAPIRequests">Combin=
ing Vision API Requests</h2>
<p>The Vision Framework allows the creation of efficient pipelines by combi=
ning multiple tasks into a single analysis. The <code>VNRequest</code> clas=
s represents these tasks and can be used with either <code>VNImageRequestHa=
ndler</code> (for still images) or <code>VNSequenceRequestHandler</code> (f=
or videos).</p>
<p>For example, face detection (<code>VNDetectFaceRectanglesRequest</code>)=
 and text recognition (<code>VNRecognizeTextRequest</code>) can be combined=
:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">try? han=
dler.perform([faceRequest, textRequest]</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>These distinct requests are executed together via the <code>perform(_:)<=
/code> function, optimizing processor usage and consolidating results.</p>
<p>It=E2=80=99s also possible to limit the analysis with <code>regionOfInte=
rest</code>, which defines a specific area of the image:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">request.=
regionOfInterest =3D CGRect(x: 0.25, y: 0.25, width: 0.5, height: 0.5)</pre=
>
</div>
</div>
<p>This saves resources and focuses detection on relevant regions, such as =
the center of the screen.</p>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-IntegrationwithCoreML">Integration=
 with Core ML</h2>
<p>Custom machine learning models can be used with Vision. To ensure that i=
nference is fast and suitable for real-time processing, it's important to a=
pply <strong>latency reduction</strong> techniques.</p>
<p>A common way to reduce latency is to convert the model to lighter numeri=
c types such as <code>float16</code> or <code>int8</code>, which shortens c=
omputation time with minimal accuracy loss. Another useful practice is to a=
void unnecessarily deep or heavy layers in the machine learning model.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Prepare the model in Core ML format (using Create ML or <code>coremltool=
s</code>).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Optimize to reduce latency (float16 or int8).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use <code>VNCoreMLModel</code> and <code>VNCoreMLRequest</code>:</p></li=
>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">let mode=
l =3D try? VNCoreMLModel(for: MyCustomModel().model)
let mlRequest =3D VNCoreMLRequest(model: model!, completionHandler: handleM=
LResults)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>These classes support direct inference on processed image data.</p>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-PerformanceandEfficienc">Performan=
ce and Efficienc</h2>
<p>Processing images in real time requires careful attention to performance=
:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Run requests on <strong>background threads</strong> using <code>Dispatch=
Queue.global</code> to avoid freezing the interface.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Analyze only <strong>a few frames per second</strong> using <code>CADisp=
layLink</code> or <code>Timer</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reduce <strong>input resolution</strong> to speed up processing with min=
imal accuracy loss.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reuse the <code>VNSequenceRequestHandler</code> whenever possible to avo=
id unnecessary reinitialization.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-TestingandValidation">Testing and =
Validation</h2>
<p>Ensuring application quality involves testing not only whether the code =
works, but also whether it performs well under different conditions.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Simulate image variations (low light, different angles) using <strong>XC=
Test</strong>, Xcode=E2=80=99s native testing framework. It enables automat=
ed verification of functionalities, detection of failures, and ensures that=
 future updates don=E2=80=99t break existing features.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Measure performance with <strong>Instruments &gt; Time Profiler</strong>=
, a Xcode tool that analyzes where execution time is being spent in your co=
de. This helps identify performance bottlenecks and optimize image processi=
ng and Vision Framework calls.*</p></li>
<li>
<p>Adjust requests, image size, and analysis frequency as needed to balance=
 accuracy and speed, ensuring a smooth user experience.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-PrivacyandCompliance">Privacy and =
Compliance</h2>
<p>Declare camera usage in <code>Info.plist</code>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">&lt;key&=
gt;NSCameraUsageDescription&lt;/key&gt;
&lt;string&gt;We use the camera to detect faces and recognize text.&lt;/str=
ing&gt;</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>If data is sent to servers, use encryption (File Protection and Keychain=
) and obtain user consent.</p>
<h2 id=3D"BestPracticesforComputerVision-Conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p>Following best practices in using the Vision Framework, from architectur=
e to performance and privacy, ensures your application is more reliable, fa=
st, and user-focused. The combination of requests, efficient image handling=
, and Core ML integration paves the way for intelligent computer vision sol=
utions.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
